\begin{proof}
($\implies$) Suppose A is equilateral. By translation invariance, we may consider translating A such that it is centred on the origin, then substituting $b = ae^{i2\pi/3}$, $c=ce^{i4\pi/3}$ shows that the relationship holds trivially.
